{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1119454-werewolves-and-mental-gifts-disciplines","id":1119454,"title":"Werewolves and mental gifts/disciplines.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-23T03:58:15-07:00","id":1119454,"title":"Werewolves and mental gifts/disciplines.","content":"Can a werewolf resist mental gifts or disciplines? In the case of Magick, they do have an innate countermagick die so that's alright, not what I'm asking here. I'm asking for the possibility of resisting such attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12188-theexplosivearrow","name":"TheExplosiveArrow","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T13:03:20-07:00","id":1119613,"title":"","content":"Werewolves don't have any innate abilities (though lots of things don't work on a Frenzying werewolf) for resisting mental powers beyond whatever restrains the abilities in question (such as Dominate difficulties being based on the target's Willpower).<br /> <br /> There are Merits, Gifts, and etc. that can aid in this. Ragabash and Gnawer Gifts are good places to look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T18:21:54-07:00","id":1119717,"title":"","content":"The Gifts are actually all over the place. Silver Fangs have a nigh no-sell in the form of Mindblock (set difficulty to 10), and there's a Level Two Stargazer Gift, Resist Temptation, that can make it really difficult (it's also a general Gift for the Beast Courts). The Metis gift Shell actually no-sells those effects, at the cost of sealing off Rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T18:54:31-07:00","id":1119731,"title":"","content":"Which is not necessarily a bad thing if you are involved in negotiations, the real problem is that they cannot generate successes on Empathy or Primal-Urge rolls, which can be a hindrance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}